'''Star Circle''' is the [[frequent-flyer program|frequent flyer program]] of [[Aeroístmus]], the flag carrier of [[Balboa]]. Launched in 2008, the program uses a spend-based earning model, awarding members 5 [[Aero Points]] per $1 spent on base fares and carrier surcharges. Star Circle is a full member of the [[Adonian Arrow]] airline alliance, allowing members to earn and redeem Aero Points across all alliance partner flights, including codeshare services operated by [[Sanesair]].

== Earning ==

=== Flight earning ===

Members earn 5 Aero Points per $1 spent on the base fare and carrier-imposed surcharges of any Aeroístmus ticket. Government taxes and airport fees are excluded from point earning. Elite tier members receive a bonus multiplier on top of the base earn rate:

{| class="wikitable"
|+ Elite earning multipliers
|-
! Tier !! Bonus
|-
| Member || 0%
|-
| Silver || +25%
|-
| Gold || +75%
|-
| Platinum || +100%
|-
| Diamond || +150%
|}

For example, a Gold member purchasing a $2,000 round-trip ticket from [[Sant Cristòfor International Airport|Sant Cristòfor]] to [[Aoyama-Maekawa International Airport|Aoyama-Maekawa]] earns 10,000 base points plus a 75% elite bonus of 7,500 points, for a total of 17,500 Aero Points.

=== Credit card earning ===

[[Banc Balboa]] issues a co-branded Star Circle credit card in three tiers. Cardholders earn Aero Points on all purchases, with elevated earn rates on Aeroístmus spend. Points earned through credit card spending do not count toward elite tier qualification. The Platinum card confers automatic Gold elite status upon account opening, subject to maintenance of the card account.

{| class="wikitable"
|+ Banc Balboa Star Circle card earn rates
|-
! Card tier !! Aeroístmus spend !! Everyday spend !! Elite status
|-
| Standard || 3 pts/$1 || 1 pt/$1 || None
|-
| Gold || 5 pts/$1 || 1 pt/$1 || None
|-
| Platinum || 10 pts/$1 || 1.5 pts/$1 || Automatic Gold
|}

=== Partner earning ===

Aero Points can be earned through non-airline partners:

{| class="wikitable"
|+ Non-air partners
|-
! Partner !! Type !! Earn rate
|-
| [[Grup Pastel]] || Hotels and resorts || 2 pts/$1
|-
| [[IstmeLloguer]] || Car rental || 1 pt/$1
|-
| [[HRX]] || Retail (transfer partner) || 1:1 point transfer
|}

[[Grup Pastel]] is Balboa's largest hospitality and tourism group, operating 42 properties across the isthmus. [[IstmeLloguer]] (Lloguer i Viatges de l'Istme, S.A.) is the country's principal car rental operator, with 12 locations nationwide and a fleet of approximately 4,200 vehicles. [[HRX]] is Balboa's largest department store and retail company; Star Circle members may transfer HRX loyalty points to Aero Points at a 1:1 ratio.

== Tiers ==

Star Circle operates a four-tier elite structure above base membership. Qualification is points-based, with no segment-count alternative. The qualification period follows the calendar year (January to December). There is no soft landing policy; members who fail to requalify revert to base membership.

{| class="wikitable"
|+ Tier qualification and benefits
|-
! Tier !! Points required !! Earning bonus !! Key benefits
|-
| Member || 0 || 0% || Earn and redeem, standard baggage allowance
|-
| Silver || 25,000 || +25% || Priority check-in, one extra bag, priority boarding
|-
| Gold || 50,000 || +75% || Lounge access, upgrade priority
|-
| Platinum || 75,000 || +100% || Extra baggage, priority security, companion lounge access (1 guest)
|-
| Diamond || 125,000 || +150% || Guaranteed seat, invitation events
|}

=== Companion lounge access ===

Platinum and Diamond members may bring one guest into the lounge at no additional cost. Lower-tier members do not receive companion lounge access.

=== Lifetime status ===

Star Circle offers lifetime elite status based on total lifetime Aero Points earned:

