== Redemption ==

=== Award chart ===

Star Circle uses a zone-based award chart with one-way pricing. Round-trip redemptions are priced as two one-way awards. Any seat on any flight is available for award redemption; there are no blackout dates and no restricted award inventory.

The award chart comprises three geographic zones:

{| class="wikitable"
|+ One-way award chart (Aero Points)
|-
! Zone !! Economy !! Premium Economy !! Business !! First
|-
| Domestic (Balboa) || 8,000 || 12,000 || 16,000 || 24,000
|-
| Lurandia + Abyala || 20,000 || 30,000 || 40,000 || 60,000
|-
| Fosia / Illypnia / Kaftia || 40,000 || 60,000 || 80,000 || 120,000
|}

Cabin class multipliers are applied as follows: economy 1×, premium economy 1.5×, business 2×, and first 3× the economy award price.

=== Alliance redemption ===

Aero Points may be redeemed for award flights on all [[Adonian Arrow]] alliance member airlines, including [[Sanesair]] codeshare services. Award pricing on partner flights follows the same zone-based chart.

=== Cabin upgrades ===

Members may use Aero Points to upgrade from economy to a higher cabin class. Upgrades are available only on full-fare economy tickets; discounted or restricted economy fares are not eligible for upgrade awards.

=== Point expiry ===

Aero Points do not expire as long as the member's account remains active. An account is considered active if the member completes at least one flight on Aeroístmus or any Adonian Arrow partner airline within any 24-month period. Accounts are individual; household or family point pooling is not offered.

